# Copy to .env and adjust. Never commit the real .env file (it is gitignored), and never put real
# secrets in docker-compose.yml, the Dockerfile or CI config -- see docs/operations/ci-cd.md for
# where each secret lives in staging/production.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ core
# development (default) | staging | production. staging/production turn on a startup guard that
# REFUSES to boot with the public demo JWT secret, the no-login token endpoint, or default CORS
# origins -- so a deployed service can't quietly run insecurely.
ATLAS_ENV=development
ATLAS_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
ATLAS_LOG_FORMAT=console   # `json` in containers/deployments (one searchable object per line)

# Signing secret for operator tokens. REQUIRED (and >= 32 chars, not the demo value) outside
# development. Generate one:  python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"
# ATLAS_JWT_SECRET=
# Browser origin(s) of the dashboard allowed to call the API (comma-separated). REQUIRED outside
# development, e.g. https://atlas-staging.example.com
# ATLAS_DASHBOARD_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
# Port to listen on (platforms such as Render/Cloud Run set PORT themselves). Default 8000.
# PORT=8000
# ATLAS_API_PORT=8000   # same thing, for platforms that don't inject PORT; PORT wins if both are set

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ optional features
# Keep incident history (incl. ones awaiting approval) across API restarts. Opt-in.
# ATLAS_STATE_DB=data/state/atlas.sqlite
# Set to 0 to run the API without the live traffic simulation (approval workflow only).
# ATLAS_LIVE_TRAFFIC=1
# Which network the demo API simulates: the Midtown district (default) or a built city under
# data/networks/<name>/ (e.g. `manhattan`: all ~2,670 signals, libsumo, teleporting on, what-if off).
# ATLAS_NETWORK=manhattan_midtown
# City mode only: fraction of the generated demand to simulate. 0.25 keeps a 4-core laptop above
# real time; 1.0 is the full generated demand (measured ~0.8x real time on such a laptop).
# ATLAS_DEMAND_SCALE=0.25
# Local convenience only: the dashboard's "Get demo token" button. `make demo` sets it; the
# startup guard forbids it in staging/production.
# ATLAS_DEMO_AUTH=1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ error monitoring (optional)
# Sentry stays OFF unless this is set (and the image/venv has `--extra observability`). No PII and
# no request bodies are sent. Release/environment are tagged automatically.
# SENTRY_DSN=
# SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=0

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ LLM playbook proposals (optional)
# With no keys the deterministic mapper is used. Keys go ONLY in your local .env or the platform's
# secret manager -- never in the repo, never pasted in chat.
GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Free-tier caps differ per model and change; set what YOUR account shows. Defaults are conservative.
# ATLAS_GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
# ATLAS_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# ATLAS_GROQ_RPM=30
# ATLAS_GROQ_RPD=14400
# ATLAS_GEMINI_RPM=10
# ATLAS_GEMINI_RPD=250
# Shared rate-limit state (docker compose --profile app up); in-memory fallback if unreachable.
# ATLAS_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ RL policy (optional)
# A trained MAPPO policy (see docs/training/kaggle.md) -> adds an "RL policy" mode to every junction.
# Loading says nothing about quality; evaluate with scripts/run_evaluation_pilot.py --rl-checkpoint <file>.
# ATLAS_RL_CHECKPOINT=data/models/mappo_district.pt
